ders. Data-centre grid connection requests are growing 9% in 2027, which is slower than in 2026.\n- **Financing (n3):** The financing is only partly secured. Debt is open to the stronger utilities, but bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp. Equity is not dependable: Pellham withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering after investor demand fell short, and it scaled back procurement. Some 2027 capex will probably be deferred, with Pellham most at risk. That puts part of the demand growth in doubt, and it is the main reason to hold back.\n- **Price (n4):** The LEAPS are fairly priced, not cheap. Implied volatility is 27%, against a 2-year median of 26%. Price gives no reason to add now, and no reason to avoid it.\n\nThe demand case is real, but the Pellham financing problem puts part of it at risk. Waiting costs little because the options are not cheap. I would add more if one of these happens:\n- Pellham's financing is resolved.\n- Implied volatility falls below its median.\n- Utility orders confirm the capex plans.\n\nI read the three nodes' headline findings and the source lines that came through. I did not independently check the underlying documents. This is not personalised financial advice.","ttft_ms":2196,"type":"result","duration_ms":34320,"uuid":"9df7c000-0979-4623-a2e0-433242cb85fc","ttft_stream_ms":1405,"time_to_request_ms":303,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":43,"system_prompt":32,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":21,"input_attachments":42,"input_hooks":14,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":24,"tool_pool_refresh":17,"init_message":18,"init_frame_send":8,"engine_pickup":4,"loop_entry":16,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":10,"request_announcements":31,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":6,"tool_schema_build":4,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":4,"request_build":4},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":93,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":73,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss